<main class="main-content" id="main-content">
<div class="source-breadcrumb"><a href="/source-games/">Source Games</a><span aria-hidden="true"> / </span>Team Fortress 2</div>
<header class="tf2-heading"><div><span class="source-kicker">SOURCE · TWO EDITIONS</span><div class="product-heading"><h1>Team Fortress 2</h1><span class="product-status is-free">Free preview</span></div><p class="product-intro">Your game. Your team. Your version.</p></div><div class="tf2-version"><label for="tf2-edition">Game version</label><select id="tf2-edition"><option value="tf2">Team Fortress 2</option><option value="tf2-classified">TF2 Classified</option></select></div></header>
<section class="tf2-hero" aria-label="Selected TF2 edition"><img class="tf2-scene" src="/assets/images/tf2/background-v1.webp" alt="" width="1672" height="941" fetchpriority="high"><div class="tf2-hero-content"><img id="tf2-logo" src="/assets/images/tf2/tf2-logo-transparent-v1.png" alt="Team Fortress 2" width="739" height="249"><div class="tf2-hero-caption"><span>WINDOWS x64</span><span>FREE ACCESS</span></div></div></section>
<div class="tf2-details"><section aria-labelledby="tf2-about"><span class="source-kicker">PICK YOUR SIDE</span><h2 id="tf2-about">Team Fortress 2</h2><p id="tf2-description" aria-live="polite">The original nine-class battlefield. Choose retail TF2 for the Steam version of Team Fortress 2.</p><p>Both editions are free for signed-in Scooby users. Each keeps its own game process, files, settings and scripts.</p><div class="tf2-actions"><a class="purchase-btn" href="/download/">Get Scooby Launcher <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="purchase-btn secondary" href="#setup">Setup guide</a></div><p class="tf2-note">Preview builds are in development. Windows x64 only; complete feature parity and other platforms have not been verified.</p></section><section class="tf2-steps" id="setup" aria-labelledby="tf2-setup"><span class="source-kicker">GET STARTED</span><h2 id="tf2-setup">One launcher. Two versions.</h2><ol><li><strong>Sign in to Scooby.</strong><span>Open TF2 from Home or Source Games.</span></li><li><strong>Choose your game.</strong><span>Select TF2 or TF2 Classified in the popup. “Don’t show again” remembers your choice.</span></li><li><strong>Press Load.</strong><span>Enable Start game to open the selected game with the required launch options. If it is already running, launch it with <code>-insecure</code> first.</span></li><li><strong>Make it yours.</strong><span>Use Insert or F1 in game. You can always switch versions using the dashboard dropdown.</span></li></ol></section></div>
<section class="tf2-feature-section" id="features" aria-labelledby="tf2-features"><span class="source-kicker">IN THE PREVIEW</span><h2 id="tf2-features">A familiar set of tools.</h2><div class="tf2-features"><article><h3>Player visuals</h3><p>ESP, health and labels, with independent visible and invisible chams controls.</p></article><article><h3>Movement & view</h3><p>Movement helpers, camera controls and edition-specific settings in the shared Scooby interface.</p></article><article><h3>Lua & profiles</h3><p>Save settings and work with Lua scripts. Each game retains its own data and capabilities.</p></article></div></section>
</main>
